<title>MEXICO: Mexico Nov 96 coffee exports edge higher vs Nov 95.</title>
<headline>Mexico Nov 96 coffee exports edge higher vs Nov 95.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico exported 320,843 60-kg bags of coffee in November 1996 compared to the 296,510 bags sold abroad in the same month a year earlier, the Mexican Coffee Council said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The exports amount to a further consoilidation of the solid start to the Mexican October-September coffee export cycle for 1996-1997.</p>
<p>In the first two months of the current cycle, exports have totaled 484,332 bags versus the 428,422 bags in the previous cycle. A breakdown per month of comparative cycles follows. Exports are in 60-kg bags. Figures are updated.  </p>
<p>    Month		     1995-1996		 1996-1997</p>
<p>    October		    131,912		   163,489</p>
<p>    November		   296,510		   320,843</p>
<p>    December		   421,445		     N/A</p>
<p>    January		    745,428		     N/A</p>
<p>    February		   742,615		     N/A</p>
<p>    March			831,513		     N/A</p>
<p>    April			529,015		     N/A</p>
<p>    May			  456,195		     N/A</p>
<p>    June			 193,293		     N/A</p>
<p>    July			 219,432		     N/A</p>
<p>    August		     146,745		     N/A</p>
<p>    September		   92,554		     N/A</p>
<p>    Total		    4,578,857		   484,332*</p>
<p>* Total to date.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.</p>
